# scripts/opcount: `tailbench bench trylet N` makes N calls of a function that
# passes a fallible call's failure on through a try (INLINE-FAIL-LOCAL), its
# failures caught in the loop. The control is the same in hand Go: an
# `if err != nil { return 0, err }` and a type switch.
unit call
sizes 409600 2457600
args bench trylet {n}
control benchmarks/tailcall/testdata/control
